Deployment — install pipeline, releases, systemd lifecycle

Context

End users need a one-command install: `curl -fsSL install.imaginarystorage.com | sudo bash`. The project ships as a single C binary plus a Vite-built React bundle, runs as root for fork+setuid, and is managed by systemd in production. This entry documents the entire pipeline from `VERSION` file to a working installed service, so future maintenance and the next release cycle don't require relearning any of it.

Branch: `feat/deployment` (merged to main as of 2026-05-19).
First release: `v0.1.0` (lacks bundled `install.sh` asset — see Gotchas).
Working release: `v0.1.1` and onward.

---

Versioning

`VERSION` at the repo root holds a single line like `0.1.0`. Both halves of the codebase derive their version from this one file.

Backend
- `Makefile` reads `VERSION` and `git rev-parse --short HEAD` at build time and passes them as `-DIMAGINARY_VERSION`, `-DIMAGINARY_GIT_SHA`, `-DIMAGINARY_BUILD_AT` into all object files.
- Only `src/routes/version.c` actually consumes those macros. To stop `bump.sh patch && make` from being a no-op (no `.c` file changed, so make reuses old `.o`), the Makefile has an explicit dependency: `$(BUILD_DIR)/src/routes/version.o: VERSION`.
- New endpoint: `GET /version` (public, unauthenticated) → `{ "version", "commit", "built_at" }`.
- Liveness probe: `GET /healthz` (public) → `200 OK ok` plain text.

Frontend
- `frontend/vite.config.ts` reads `../VERSION` synchronously and exposes it via `define: { __APP_VERSION__: JSON.stringify(version) }`.
- `frontend/src/vite-env.d.ts` declares `declare const __APP_VERSION__: string;`.
- Version shown in sidebar footer as muted `v0.1.0` text.
- `frontend/src/lib/versionCheck.ts` — boot-time hook that fetches `/version` once, compares to `__APP_VERSION__`, and toasts a Reload-action prompt if they disagree. Hook gated by a module-level `alreadyChecked` flag so React StrictMode's double-mount doesn't fire two toasts.

Bumping
- `scripts/bump.sh major|minor|patch|set <X.Y.Z>|--print` — edits `VERSION` atomically. Never commits/tags. Validates the result.
- Release flow: `scripts/bump.sh patch && git commit -am "chore: release v$(cat VERSION)" && scripts/release.sh`.

---

Releases

`scripts/release.sh`
- Guards: clean tree, current branch == `main` (override: `--allow-branch`), tag not already present locally or on `origin`.
- Tags annotated as `v$(cat VERSION)`, pushes to `origin`.
- Confirms before tagging unless `--yes`.
- Prints CI + Releases URLs derived from `git remote.origin.url`.
- Gotcha that bit us: `git log --pretty | head -20` fails under `set -o pipefail` because `head` closes its stdin (SIGPIPE) after 20 lines. Fixed by using `git log -n 20` directly. Lesson: avoid `| head` in pipefail scripts.

`.github/workflows/release.yml`
- Triggered by `push: tags: ['v*']`.
- Jobs (in order): `verify` → `build-server` (matrix: x86_64, aarch64) + `build-frontend` (parallel) → `package` (matrix: x86_64, aarch64) → `release`.
- `verify` reads `VERSION` and aborts if `v$(cat VERSION) != $GITHUB_REF_NAME` — catches "I tagged but forgot to bump VERSION".
- Runners: `ubuntu-22.04` and `ubuntu-22.04-arm`. Deliberately not `ubuntu-latest`: 22.04 gives glibc 2.35, which lets binaries run on Debian 12, Ubuntu 22.04+, Arch, Fedora 37+.
- Builds with `make VERSION=… GIT_SHA=…` (explicit pass for CI clarity, the Makefile would pick them up either way).
- `strip dist/server` — drops ~30% off the binary, no runtime impact.
- Vite outputs to `../www`, so the workflow uploads `path: www` (the original draft pointed at the non-existent `frontend/dist/`).
- Each `package` job assembles `imaginary-storage-v<ver>/{bin,web,etc,VERSION,README.md,install.sh,uninstall.sh}` and produces `imaginary-storage-v<ver>-linux-<arch>.tar.gz` + `.sha256`.
- `release` job: combines per-arch sha files into `imaginary-storage-v<ver>-SHA256SUMS`, attaches tarballs + sums + `install.sh` + `uninstall.sh` to the GitHub Release, sets `generate_release_notes: true`.

Release-asset gotcha
- v0.1.0 was published without `install.sh`/`uninstall.sh` as standalone release assets — they were inside the tarball but the docs advertised `curl …/releases/latest/download/install.sh`, which 404'd. Fixed in v0.1.1 by adding them to the `files:` list of `softprops/action-gh-release@v2` and adding `actions/checkout@v4` to the release job (the action needs the files on disk).

