Install / uninstall scripts

`install.sh`
- One script, two invocation modes:
  - **Remote**: `curl -fsSL install.imaginarystorage.com | sudo bash` (or the legacy long URL).
  - **Local**: extract a tarball, `sudo ./install.sh`. Detected by `[ -f VERSION ] && [ -x bin/server ]` in `$(dirname "$0")`.
- Flags: `--version vX.Y.Z`, `--prefix /path`, `--port N`, `--no-start`, `--yes`/`-y`, `--help`.
- Preflight: requires root; arch detect (`x86_64`/`aarch64`); checks `libpam`/`libacl` via `ldconfig -p`; requires `tar curl sha256sum systemctl`.
- Resolves version: `--version` override or `curl …/releases/latest` and grep `tag_name` from the API JSON.
- Downloads tarball + `imaginary-storage-v<ver>-SHA256SUMS` to a `mktemp -d`, verifies with `sha256sum -c`, extracts.
- Upgrade detection: reads `/opt/imaginary-storage/VERSION` if present. Same version → confirm reinstall. Different → upgrade path. Stops the service before swapping files.
- Installs files:
  - `/opt/imaginary-storage/{bin,web,etc,VERSION,README.md}` — wholesale replace (rm -rf web then copy) so removed assets don't linger.
- First-install only: writes `/etc/imaginary-storage/config.env` with `IMAGINARY_PORT`, `IMAGINARY_WEB_ROOT`, `IMAGINARY_DATA_DIR`, plus commented TLS placeholders. Upgrades never touch this file.
- Creates `/var/lib/imaginary-storage/sessions/` (mode 0700, root-owned).
- Installs systemd unit at `/etc/systemd/system/imaginary-storage.service`, `daemon-reload`, `enable --now` (skip with `--no-start`).
- Prints URL + status hint on success.
- Help block is rendered by `sed -n '3,25p' "$0" | sed 's/^# \{0,1\}//'`. The line range is brittle — if the file's top comment grows or shrinks, update the range or `--help` will print junk. (Already fixed twice during this work.)

`uninstall.sh`
- `--purge` removes `/etc/imaginary-storage` + `/var/lib/imaginary-storage`. Default leaves them alone.
- **Never** touches `~/.imaginary/` in any user's home — that's user-owned data (bookmarks, settings, trash, upload temp).
- Idempotent: stop+disable wrapped in `|| true` so a half-installed state still cleans up.

