Server changes for service-mode

Most of the wiring lives in `src/main.c`. Three runtime knobs are read from env at startup:

| Env var               | Default (dev) | Service value                                |
|-----------------------|---------------|----------------------------------------------|
| `IMAGINARY_PORT`      | `8080`        | from `config.env` (default still 8080)       |
| `IMAGINARY_DATA_DIR`  | `.`           | `/var/lib/imaginary-storage`                 |
| `IMAGINARY_WEB_ROOT`  | `www`         | `/opt/imaginary-storage/web`                 |

`g_session_dir` (was a `#define SESSION_DIR "./sessions"` in `auth/auth.h`) is now an `extern const char *` set at startup from `${IMAGINARY_DATA_DIR}/sessions`. Same pattern for `g_web_root` replacing `#define STATIC_ROOT "www"` in `routes/static.c`.

Graceful shutdown
- `volatile sig_atomic_t g_shutting_down = 0` defined in `main.c`, declared `extern` from `lib/chttp.c`.
- `on_term(SIGTERM)` and `on_term(SIGINT)` set the flag and call `shutdown(g_server_fd, SHUT_RDWR)` to wake the blocking `accept()`.
- `chttp_server_run()` checks `g_shutting_down` after each `accept()` and breaks. Errors from `accept()`: `EINTR` is `continue`, anything else with the flag set is a clean break.
- `SIGPIPE` is `SIG_IGN` so a client hangup mid-write doesn't kill the server.

systemd unit (`etc/imaginary-storage.service`)
- `User=root`, `Type=simple`, `EnvironmentFile=-/etc/imaginary-storage/config.env`, `ExecStart=/opt/imaginary-storage/bin/server`.
- `Restart=on-failure`, `RestartSec=2s`, `TimeoutStopSec=30s`.
- `After=network-online.target` + `Wants=network-online.target`.
- Hardening compatible with the fork+setuid model: `ProtectSystem=full`, `ProtectKernelTunables=yes`, `ProtectKernelModules=yes`, `ProtectControlGroups=yes`. Notes:
  - `NoNewPrivileges` is OFF (breaks setuid).
  - `ProtectHome` is OFF (we read user homes).
  - `PrivateUsers` is OFF (breaks setuid).
- Installer overwrites this unit on every upgrade. Local overrides go in `/etc/systemd/system/imaginary-storage.service.d/override.conf` via `systemctl edit imaginary-storage` (e.g., `RequiresMountsFor=/mnt/nas` to wait for an external disk).

