install.imaginarystorage.com — Cloudflare Worker

`workers/install/` contains a small Worker that proxies the latest `install.sh` so the curl command stays short.

- `src/index.js`: on `/` or `/install.sh`, fetch `https://github.com/imaginary-storage/NAS/releases/latest/download/install.sh` and stream its body back with `Content-Type: text/x-shellscript` and a 5-minute edge cache. Browser visits to `/` (detected by `Accept: text/html`) get an HTML landing page with the install command instead.
- `wrangler.toml`: binds the Worker to `install.imaginarystorage.com/*` on the `imaginarystorage.com` zone. Cloudflare provisions the proxied DNS record automatically.
- Deploy: `cd workers/install && wrangler deploy` (requires `wrangler login` against the account owning the zone).
- We chose proxy-not-redirect deliberately: a 302 from the Worker would force users to remember `curl -L`. Streaming the body means bare `curl install.imaginarystorage.com | bash` works.
- The Worker has no secrets, no state. Cloudflare free tier covers this trivially (GitHub Releases serves the actual bytes; Worker just relays headers).

If Cloudflare ever goes away
- Fallback URL is `https://github.com/imaginary-storage/NAS/releases/latest/download/install.sh`. It's a real asset on every release ≥ v0.1.1.

