Operational notes

After bumping `VERSION` locally
- `make` will recompile `src/routes/version.c` (and only that) thanks to the explicit Makefile dependency. Restart `./run server` or whatever's running.
- If the SPA is also rebuilt against the new `VERSION`, the boot-time mismatch toast disappears.

The mismatch toast
- It compares `data.version` from `/version` (whatever the running binary baked in) with `__APP_VERSION__` (what the SPA was bundled with). If they disagree, it usually means one half was rebuilt and the other wasn't. Most common cause during dev: forgot to restart the server after a bump.

`./run server`
- Builds the binary (`make`), builds the frontend (`cd frontend && npm run build`), then `sudo ./dist/server`. The frontend build emits to `www/` (Vite's `outDir: '../www'`). The server defaults `IMAGINARY_WEB_ROOT=www`, so the dev workflow works without any env setup.

Cutting a new release
1. `scripts/bump.sh patch` (or `minor`/`major`/`set X.Y.Z`).
2. `git commit -am "chore: release v$(cat VERSION)"`.
3. `git push origin main` if not yet pushed.
4. `scripts/release.sh` (or `--allow-branch --yes` if tagging off a non-main branch).
5. Watch CI: `gh run watch <id>` or visit Actions. Build is ~2 minutes.
6. `curl -fsSL install.imaginarystorage.com | sudo bash` against a Linux VM to smoke-test (only do this once the Worker is deployed; pre-Worker it was the long GitHub URL).

What to do if a release goes wrong
- The tag is on the commit, the build is reproducible from the tag. Easiest fix is to bump VERSION and cut a `v0.1.N+1`. Don't try to re-publish over the same tag — softprops/action-gh-release will refuse, and even if it didn't, mirrors/caches would diverge.
- To delete a bad release entirely: `gh release delete vX.Y.Z --yes && git push origin :refs/tags/vX.Y.Z && git tag -d vX.Y.Z`.

